1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,400
Ana wants to rent an apartment
in Passo Fundo.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,600
Her landlord wants a guarantor.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:09,800
MUTAV is that guarantor,
and its reserve runs on Solana.

4
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:14,900
Her agency works in MUTAV's platform;
every lease becomes an account on-chain.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,600
Our operator puts Ana's lease on-chain:
R$18,000 of cover,

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,500
an opaque ID, no personal data.

7
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,200
Anyone can watch the reserve:
what it holds in BRS,

8
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:35,000
Nora's Brazilian real stablecoin,
and what it must hold.

9
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:36,900
The rule is code.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
One more lease would need R$45,000;
the reserve holds R$44,000.

11
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:46,400
Refused.

12
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:50,000
MUTAV can't promise
what its reserve can't back.

13
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,800
Now say Ana misses a month.

14
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,600
The operator files the claim,

15
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:09,600
the reserve pays
within the admin's cap,

16
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:15,600
and the PIX to the agency
is recorded on-chain.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,400
On-chain, filed to settled
in [N] seconds.

18
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:28,200
Seguro-fiança allows
up to thirty days.

19
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:40,200
Because the reserve keeps a quarter
of what it guarantees,

20
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:44,900
every real of capital can back
up to four in cover

21
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:46,600
and earn its fees.

22
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:51,400
Even after Ana's claim,
each share is worth more.

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,400
The same reserve that protects
the landlord pays the people who fund it.

24
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,800
MUTAV: a transparent,
programmable reserve,

25
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,600
claims settled in minutes,
capital that works.

26
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,400
Brazil's onchain rent guarantee.
